<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percurso</span></b> , āre, v.
			freq. a. and n.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to run</i> or <i>range through</i>, <i>ramble over</i>
			(perh. not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ripas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Pan. 12, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to range</i> or <i>rove about</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">finibus nostris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 42, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
